@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/world/simulation#> .
@prefix actuation: <http://example.org/orexis/actuation#> .
@prefix reporting: <http://example.org/orexis/reporting#> .
@prefix ag: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix market: <http://example.org/orexis/market#> .
@prefix sensing: <http://example.org/orexis/sensing#> .
@prefix desire: <http://example.org/orexis/desire#> .
@prefix ssn:  <http://www.w3.org/ns/ssn/> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix water: <http://example.org/orexis/water#> .
@prefix intention: <http://example.org/orexis/intention#> .

#  The supplier's PRIVATE beliefs — the DEALER's terms: a genuine seller downstream, a genuine
#  buyer upstream, and the barrel between them.
#
#  It composed market:Hosting, actuation:Actuation, sensing:Listening (arc 1), the stake
#  quartet desire/intention/deliberation (arc 2) and — since the city exists — market:Bidding
#  (arc 4), so those modules' terms appear and no others. There is still no cadence: the one
#  thing it perceives announces on its own clock.

##  market:Hosting — how it runs a round
:supplier
    market:offerQuantityL 2.0 ;      # what it puts up
    market:reservePricePerL 0.20 ;   # its floor; buyers never see the reasoning
    market:bidWindowS 3 ;            # how long it waits for bids before matching
    market:roundCooldownS 30 .       # it will not open rounds faster than this

##  actuation:Actuation — how long it waits for a valve to say it dispensed
#   Added to the open-seconds it computed for that dose, never used alone: a ninety-second
#   pour is not late at thirty. Silence past the deadline is reported and counted, never acted
#   on — the water may well have flowed and only the report been lost.
:supplier actuation:doseGraceS 10 .

##  How often it says how it is — belief base size, reading freshness, silent write failures.
#   Omit this line and the agent reports nothing; see orexis/metrics.py.
:supplier reporting:metricsIntervalS 60 .

##  sensing:Listening — the barrel's level sensor announces on its own clock (arc 1), and all
#   a listener states is how long it waits before calling the thing gone quiet.
##  intention — demanded the moment the stake met the valves it already held: a keeper of
#   commitments states its patience. Long, because a merchant's commitments are rounds, not
#   twitches. Its reflex proposes now (arc 4): the refill venue carries a direction for
#   StoredLitres, so a stock below the aim is an ACQUIRE — the same four lines that move a
#   fern, one level up the supply chain.
:supplier intention:patienceS 300 .

##  desire — the pick inside the region the barrel states (arc 2). Three litres: enough
#   slack to serve several rounds, comfortably above the stated reserve. Private where the
#   region is public, exactly as a fern's aim is.
:supplier ag:aims [ ssn:forProperty water:StoredLitres ; schema:value 3.0 ] .

##  market:Bidding — the DEALER's buy side (arc 4). Derived, not declared: the city's pipe
#   reaches its barrel and the barrel states a need in StoredLitres, so participation in the
#   refill market follows from the wiring. What only this file says is its terms as a BUYER:
#   the wallet it brings upstream, its conversion belief (identically 1.0 by conservation —
#   the entailed physics say so of the barrel, and this is the agent's own copy, the one it
#   would revise if it learned the barrel leaks), and its buy ceiling. THE SPREAD IS THE
#   DEALER'S LIVING and it is visible right here: it buys refill litres at up to 0.15 and
#   sells them at no less than its 0.20 reserve above — bought-at and sold-at are both signed
#   events, so the margin is a subtraction the sovereign can perform, which is fairness by
#   ledger rather than by referee (see the-market-has-no-governor).
:supplier
    market:hasEndowment 50.0 ;
    water:litresPerStoredLitre 1.0 ;
    water:maxValuePerL 0.15 .

:supplier sensing:maxReadingAgeS 300 ;
    #  Demanded of every perceiver by the shapes; for a pure listener it has no commanded
    #  interval to be relative to, so it is slack on the announcing clock and nothing more.
    sensing:readingGraceS 45 .

##  No self-review. The world gives this agent no mandate — it holds no revisable
#   setting to be given room on — so it derives no review capability and needs no
#   interval. Compaction still runs: that is the kernel's and not a capability.
